{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 117 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "f3ccb67464598ab8468d6c1f5f4f360880280deedb6ab649d1f180c37cb120c7" :edb/db-before-t 116 :edb/db-after-t 117 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533429 50 #inst "2026-10-10T07:46:35.607Z" 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186054641 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348385 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186054820 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348370 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186054820 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348371 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186054821 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348361 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186054821 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348372 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186054831 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348386 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186054831 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348447 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186054831 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348448 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186055504 1068 #edb/ref 17592186054231 13194139533429 17592186045585 false] [17592186055504 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347731 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186055504 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186055504 1071 "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nN,\\,Z,\\,Q,\\,R,\\,C\n$$\n\nTo which of these sets does the number $-5$ belong?" 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186055504 1071 "Consider the following sets:\n\n$N, Z, Q, R, C$\n\nTo which of these sets does the number $-5$ belong?" 13194139533429 17592186045585 false] [17592186055504 1074 "![](images/67/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- The number $-5$ is negative, so it does *not* belong to $N,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-5\\notin N.\n$$\n\n- However, $-5$ is an integer, so it does belong to $Z,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-5\\in Z.\n$$\n\n- Every integer is a rational, real, and complex number. Consequently, $-5$ belongs to $Q,R,$ and $C,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-5\\in Q,\\,-5\\in R,\\,-5\\in C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Z,Q,R,$ and $C.$\"" 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186055507 1068 #edb/ref 17592186054249 13194139533429 17592186045585 false] [17592186055507 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347717 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186055507 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186055507 1071 "Which of the numbers below belong to  ${R}_{0}^{-}?$\n\n- $-\\pi $\n- $\\sqrt{3}$\n- $-\\frac{4}{5}$\n- $0$" 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186055507 1071 "Which of the numbers below belong to $R_{0}^{-}$?\n\n1. $- π$\n2. $\\sqrt{3}$\n3. $-\\frac{4}{5}$\n4. $0$" 13194139533429 17592186045585 false] [17592186055507 1074 "Remember that ${R}_{0}^{-}$ is the set of all negative real numbers and $0.$\n\n- $-\\pi $ belongs to ${R}_{0}^{-}.\\,✓$\n\n- $\\sqrt{3}$ is a positive number, so it does *not* belong to ${R}_{0}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $-\\frac{4}{5}$ belongs to ${R}_{0}^{-}.\\,✓$\n\n- $0$ belongs to ${R}_{0}^{-}.\\,✓$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I, III, and IV only\"." 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186059795 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348233 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186059795 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348234 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186060412 1068 #edb/ref 17592186059064 13194139533429 17592186045585 false] [17592186060412 1068 #edb/ref 17592186348031 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186060412 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186060412 1071 "Given that $5 - \\textrm{i} = (p + \\textrm{i}q)(3 + 2\\textrm{i})$, calculate $p$ and $q$." 13194139533429 17592186045585 false] [17592186060412 1071 "Given that $5-\\text{i}=(p+\\text{i}q)(3+2\\text{i})$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186060412 1074 "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $3+2\\text{i}$ to isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-\\text{i} & =(p+\\text{i}q)(3+2\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{5-\\text{i}}{3+2\\text{i}} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(5-\\text{i})(3-2\\text{i})}{(3+2\\text{i})(3-2\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{15-3\\text{i}-10\\text{i}+2{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13-13\\text{i}}{9+4} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13-13\\text{i}}{13} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 1-\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $1=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $-1=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=1$ and $q=-1.$" 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186064169 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348218 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186064169 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348219 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186064170 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348217 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186068701 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348071 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186068701 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348072 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186068760 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348240 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186068774 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348356 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186068784 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348141 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186068784 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348142 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186068784 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348144 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186068794 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348138 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186068794 1038 #edb/ref 17