aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]-5[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7-2-5 & 4-4-0 \\\\ 6-6-0 & 7-2-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186115963 1068 #edb/ref 17592186114685 13194139533429 17592186045585 false] [17592186115963 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347781 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186115963 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186115963 1071 "The inverse of the $3 \\cdot 3$ matrix $A$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine $A^{-1}$.\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}A & I\\end{bmatrix}|= \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{1} & ↔R_{2} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2}\\end{vmatrix}:=___________; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & a & a & a \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & a & a & a \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & a & a & a\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139533429 17592186045585 false] [17592186115963 1071 "The inverse of the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${A}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 &  &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 &  &  &  \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 &  &  & \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186115963 1074 "We 