er all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186348115 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347977 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186348115 1069 "q-78772" 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186348115 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186348115 1071 "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186348115 1072 #uuid "ad44d2b4-38e0-5faa-8080-32a8feda902f" 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186348115 1074 "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}