ate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the circle and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](images/8a/8a0491010e71d24ebac54b5b8d03b1ce45f7de90a0f21ff1ea2f0c2babf4ec77.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{4}]$, we get the required arc of the circle.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the arc of the circle are \n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{4}].\n$$" 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186348172 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347770 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186348172 1069 "q-79166" 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186348172 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186348172 1071 "![](images/5a/5ac5a6ba5e7c041adfe2a36f9e7d835e8090a296cb72adffa5123f67cbed8aa3.png)\n\nThe three-quarter-circle above is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta ?$" 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186348172 1072 #uuid "1abc279b-47a1-5205-8023-6a51ec710161" 13194139533429 17592186045585 true] [17592186348172 1074 "The parametric equations of a circle  of radius $r$  centered at  the origin are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the radius $r=3.$ So, the parametric equations of the *full* circle are \n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a three-quarter-circle, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the circle and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](images/6f/6f27674dd7382f9040cdeb8e85ea35ff63e581ef5752b373aa0ab87a0b3e2f0f.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[0,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]$, we get the required three-quarter-circle.\n\